Source: sysible-obsidian-installer
Section: editors
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Sysible <maintainers@sysible.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://obsidian.md
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: sysible-obsidian-installer
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, curl, ca-certificates
Description: downloader/installer for Obsidian (proprietary; fetched from the vendor)
 Obsidian is a proprietary Markdown knowledge base with no apt repository, so
 Sysible cannot bundle it in the Workstation ISO. This tiny package instead
 downloads the latest official Obsidian .deb from the vendor
 (github.com/obsidianmd/obsidian-releases) and installs it at setup time — the
 same approach Ubuntu uses for restricted extras. Nothing proprietary is
 re-hosted by Sysible; only this installer is shipped.
 .
 Ticking "Obsidian" on the installer's Optional-apps page pulls in this package;
 its post-install step fetches and installs Obsidian, with a one-shot first-boot
 retry if the network isn't up yet. amd64 only (no official arm64 build — use
 the bundled CherryTree there).
